"""Bind each MCP credential to the origin its secret is sent to (IC-R1-12).

``origin`` is the scheme://host:port of the server URL a credential's secret
was entered for. A shared credential is pushed and probed only for its server
at that origin, and a config version that puts its server anywhere else is not
activated (services/mcp_credentials.py, org_config_writer.py).

A credential stored before the column existed is bound here when the org's
active config version sends it today (its server's entry references it by
credential_id with state active): to that entry's URL, where the gateway sends
it now. Any other credential stays unbound: it is sent nowhere until its
secret is re-entered with its server, so a rollback to a version that
references it is refused until then. A managed fagi.* credential has no URL in
the config (the gateway's catalog holds it) and is never bound.

Kept self-contained (the rules are copied, not imported) so a later change to
the service cannot change what this migration did.

On the release line this is 0057, after 0056_mcp_secrets_to_vault (INT wrote
it as 0046_mcp_credential_origin; MCP-APPS-PLAN.md ruling 4 and orchestrator
ruling R-c renumber it so the graph keeps one leaf). 0056 runs first and
stores each inline MCP secret of the active version as an active vault row
that version references, so this step binds those too: to their server's URL
in the active version, where the gateway sends them today.
"""

from urllib.parse import urlsplit

